    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Paris began as a settlement of the Gallic Parisii on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a>, became the Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutetia">Lutetia</a> after 52 BCE, and was made capital by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a> in 508.</li><li>The Capetian kings built it up from the 12th century into the political, religious and learning centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, with Notre-Dame, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a> and the University, and in 1328 it was the most populous city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>From the Revolution of 1789 through Haussmann's rebuilding, the siege and Commune of 1870–71 and the occupation of 1940–44, Paris was repeatedly the scene of upheaval and violence.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In September 1914, about 600 Paris taxis carried 6,000 soldiers to the front at the First Battle of the Marne, each taking five men, and the task was done within twenty-four hours.</p></aside>
    </section>

